{"year":"2026","sessionID":"2026GS","sessionIndex":"1","billNumber":"HB0437","billNumberShort":"H.B. 437","billNumberLong":"HB0437","fileNumber":"2026FL1184","shortTitle":"Environmental Permitting Amendments","currentSubVersion":"0","currentMinVersion":"0","primeSponsor":"SHALLD","primeSponsorName":"Rep. Shallenberger, David","primeSponsorHouse":"H","floorSponsor":"MILLNA","floorSponsorName":"Sen. Millner, Ann","floorSponsorHouse":"S","generalProvisions":"This bill creates a program for the expedited review of environmental permit applications.","highlightedProvisions":"This bill:<hr><ltbullet>defines terms;<hr><ltbullet>authorizes the Department of Environmental Quality (department) and Division of Oil, Gas, and Mining (division) to make rules to:<hr><ltbullet1>identify a permit administered by the department or division as a permit eligible for expedited review;<hr><ltbullet1>establish requirements for the expedited review process;<hr><ltbullet1>certify a qualified reviewer;<hr><ltbullet1>authorize a qualified reviewer to complete an expedited review of an eligible permit; and<hr><ltbullet1>establish the maximum number of a days for a qualified reviewer to complete an expedited review;<hr><ltbullet>requires the department and division to conduct a technical review and make a final administrative decision for a permit application upon completion of an expedited review; and<hr><ltbullet>makes technical and conforming changes.","moniesAppropriated":"None","draftingAttorney":"Ryan C. Williams","fiscalAnalyst":"Lacey K. Moore","lastAction":"Governor Signed","lastActionOwner":"Lieutenant Governor's office for filing","lastActionDate":"3/25/2026","trackingID":"NUGQDEHVPY","actionHistoryList":[{"description":"Bill Numbered but not Distributed","owner":"Legislative Research and General Counsel","actionDate":"2026-01-30 10:11:42.307","actionClass":"L","voteID":"","voiceVote":"","voteHouse":"","voteStr":"","actionCode":"LNUMBER","parm1":"","parm2":""},{"description":"Numbere